diff --git a/features/todo-editing.feature b/features/todo-editing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7e992db
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+Feature: Todo editing
+  As a user
+  I want to edit an existing todo title
+  So that I can correct or update my task descriptions
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded in a browser
+    And the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label activates editing mode
+    When the user double-clicks the label of "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo's list item has the "editing" class
+    And the edit input is focused and contains the title "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Save the edited title on Enter
+    Given the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user types "Buy oat milk" into the edit input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the todo title is "Buy oat milk"
+    And the todo's list item does not have the "editing" class
+
+  Scenario: Save the edited title on blur
+    Given the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user types "Buy oat milk" into the edit input
+    And the edit input loses focus
+    Then the todo title is "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: Discard changes on Escape
+    Given the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    And the user has changed the title to "Buy oat milk"
+    When the user presses Escape
+    Then the todo title remains "Buy milk"
+    And the todo's list item does not have the "editing" class
+
+  Scenario: Destroy todo when edit input is cleared
+    Given the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user clears the edit input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Destroy todo when edit input contains only whitespace
+    Given the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the user types "   " into the edit input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-filtering.feature b/features/todo-filtering.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b84b076
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-filtering.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+Feature: Todo filtering and routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by completion state
+  So that I can focus on active or completed tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded in a browser
+    And the todo list contains "Buy milk", "Walk dog", and "Write code"
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the URL hash is "#/"
+    Then the todo list shows 3 items
+    And the "All" filter link has the "selected" class
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only incomplete todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    And the items are "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    And the "Active" filter link has the "selected" class
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the item is "Walk dog"
+    And the "Completed" filter link has the "selected" class
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo in active filter hides it
+    Given the active filter is selected
+    When the user marks "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is removed from the visible list
+    And the visible list shows only "Write code"
+
+  Scenario: Uncompleting a todo in completed filter hides it
+    Given the completed filter is selected
+    When the user marks "Walk dog" as not completed
+    Then the todo "Walk dog" is removed from the visible list
+    And the visible list shows no items
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists after reload
+    Given the active filter is selected
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has the "selected" class
+    And the todo list shows only "Buy milk" and "Write code"
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-management.feature b/features/todo-management.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e8045f7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-management.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+Feature: Todo management
+  As a user
+  I want to create, complete, and clear todos
+  So that I can track my tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded in a browser
+
+  Scenario: No todos hides main and footer sections
+    Given no todos exist
+    Then the "#main" section is not visible
+    And the "#footer" section is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Create a new todo from the input field
+    Given the input field is focused
+    When the user types "Buy milk" into the new-todo input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then a new todo with the title "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And the new-todo input is cleared
+    And the "#main" section is visible
+    And the "#footer" section is visible
+
+  Scenario: Ignore empty or whitespace-only input
+    Given the input field is focused
+    When the user types "   " into the new-todo input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then no new todo is added to the list
+
+  Scenario: Mark a todo as completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" has the "completed" class on its list item
+
+  Scenario: Unmark a completed todo
+    Given the todo list contains a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" does not have the "completed" class on its list item
+
+  Scenario: Mark all todos as completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    When the user clicks the "toggle-all" checkbox
+    Then each todo has the "completed" class on its list item
+    And the "toggle-all" checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Unmark all todos via the toggle-all checkbox
+    Given all todos are completed
+    When the user clicks the "toggle-all" checkbox
+    Then no todo has the "completed" class
+    And the "toggle-all" checkbox is unchecked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all reflects individual todo completion state
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk", "Walk dog", and "Write code"
+    When the user marks "Buy milk" and "Walk dog" as completed
+    Then the "toggle-all" checkbox is not checked
+    When the user also marks "Write code" as completed
+    Then the "toggle-all" checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed todos removes only completed items
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk", "Walk dog", and "Write code"
+    And "Buy milk" and "Walk dog" are completed
+    When the user clicks the "Clear completed" button
+    Then the todo list contains exactly "Write code"
+    And the "Clear completed" button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden with no completed todos
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And no todos are completed
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Active todo count displays a pluralised counter
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    When "Walk dog" is completed
+    Then the todo-count displays "<strong>1</strong> item left"
+    When "Walk dog" is uncompleted
+    Then the todo-count displays "<strong>2</strong> items left"
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todo-persistence.feature b/features/todo-persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..60f3394
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+Feature: Todo persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to be saved across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded in a browser
+
+  Scenario: Created todos persist after reload
+    Given the user creates a todo titled "Buy milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains exactly "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Completed state persists after reload
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then "Walk dog" has the "completed" class on its list item
+    And "Buy milk" does not have the "completed" class
+
+  Scenario: Cleared completed todos stay gone after reload
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk", "Walk dog"
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+    And the user clears completed todos
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains exactly "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Edited title persists after reload
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the user changes the title of "Buy milk" to "Buy oat milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains exactly "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+    Given the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then no list item has the "editing" class
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists on reload
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+    And the user navigates to "#/active"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has the "selected" class
+    And the todo list shows only "Buy milk"
\ No newline at end of file
